9 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287644 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186285207 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287644 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186285308 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287644 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186285360 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287644 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186286206 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287644 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287644 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287644 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186285308 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287644 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f2f51709-2790-5816-b247-4202c39421bf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287680 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186287628 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287680 #edb/ref 1069 "q-181292" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287680 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287680 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is a schematic of the set ${A}^{2}$ for $A={x,y,z}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287680 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "486a4e51-6072-57cf-a504-5ca9668cfa66" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287680 #edb/ref 1074 "The set ${A}^{2}$ is equivalent to the Cartesian product ${A}^{2}=A\\times A.$\n\nThe Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nTo create a schematic of the Cartesian product $A\\times A$, we create a table and list the elements of the first set $A$ in a row across the top and the elements of the second set $A$ in a column down the left side.\n\n![](images/ad/adaba1cfa0f8aaba7638c2b581bf90ce1146f3c6ce91fa79654652bf98a2c011.png)\n\nThen, at each intersection, we write an ordered pair whose first coordinate is the corresponding element of the first set and the second coordinate is the corresponding element of the second set.\n\nOur completed $A\\times A$ schematic is shown below.\n\n![](images/91/9150fac674c8ff0608996224022243ed1a218ce077e7ccd12e7e9c8b12b732c7.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287776 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186287437 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287776 #edb/ref 1069 "q-181963" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287776 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287776 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/cb/cb3e6ef6a832f2adbbc5e096bddf2c4f6a0445fbd77a71df5617298f8dad2e51.png)\n\nBy finding the missing entries in the schematic shown above for $A\\times B,$ where $A={a,b,c}$ and $B={2,4,6},$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n- $(4,b)\\in A\\times B$\n- $(c,6)\\in A\\times B$\n- $(a,2)\\in A\\times B$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287776 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "acf6f0a0-0064-5b71-8b07-5e0f0eb96bda" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287776 #edb/ref 1074 "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nTo complete our schematic of $A\\times B,$ we write an ordered pair whose first coordinate is the corresponding element of $A$ and the second coordinate is the corresponding element of $B$ at each intersection.\n\n![](images/57/57d053cca53046f02201540e655030a37ba8f7a2811e7dc724cf30ca9fd3c072.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram:\n\n- $(4,b)\\notin A\\times B\\,\\times $\n\n- $(c,6)\\in A\\times B\\,✓$\n\n- $(a,2)\\in A\\times B\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287778 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186287532 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287778 #edb/ref 1069 "q-181969" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287778 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287778 #edb/ref 1071 "If $A={p,q,r}$ and $B={3,5},$ which of the following elements belong to $B\\times (A\\times A)?$\n\n- $(5,(r,p))$\n- $(q,(5,3))$\n- $(3,q,p)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287778 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1ec96a4e-9e05-5335-919b-b747e9d81df8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287778 #edb/ref 1074 "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, $A\\times A$ consists of every combination of ${p,q,r}$ with ${p,q,r},$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](images/aa/aad91ef7655fa8a5bf0c9852ee4e5e2166289087a56ac18e932ee3cce17164a0.png)\n\nHence, the set $A\\times A$ is given by\n\n$$\nA\\times A={(p,p),(p,q),(p,r),(q,p),(q,q),(q,r),(r,p),(r,q),(r,r)}.\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|A\\times A|=|A|\\cdot |A|=3\\cdot 3=9.\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian product\n\n$$\nB\\times (A\\times A)\n$$\n\nconsists of every combination of $B$ and $A\\times A,$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](images/e5/e573cecaa9333e071d980b1b03d65dafadd027506d2c2b9b6e8acfbe15d3be52.png)\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|B\\times (A\\times A)|=|B|\\cdot |A\\times A|=2\\cdot 9=18.\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, we see that only $(5,(r,p))\\in B\\times (A\\times A).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287789 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186287230 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287789 #edb/ref 1069 "q-182011" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287789 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287789 #edb/ref 1071 "For the sets $X={x,z},$ $Y={a,b},$ and $Z=X\\times Y,$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n- $(a,x)\\in Z$\n- $(z,a)\\in Z$\n- $(z,z)\\in Z$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287789 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4b374349-dba8-556c-833d-28419c5d38a1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287789 #edb/ref 1074 "The Cartesian product $X\\times Y$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $X$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $Y.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for $X\\times Y$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/b7/b73e7aeb017bd9f7c50f7d110c7933763834eb391ac4a3e97d25f4e587a8a3d4.png)\n\nHence, the set $Z=X\\times Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nZ={(x,a),(x,b),(z,a),(z,b)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287791 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186287419 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287791 #edb/ref 1069 "q-182015" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287791 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287791 #edb/ref 1071 "For the sets $X={5,10},$ $Y={r,s,t},$ and $Z=X\\times Y,$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n- $(5,r)\\in Z$\n- $(r,t)\\in Z$\n- $(10,s)\\in Z$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287791 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a2efc8f2-dfe5-5b29-94dc-09dde2c27a4f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287791 #edb/ref 1074 "The Cartesian product $X\\times Y$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $X$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $Y.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for $X\\times Y$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/1e/1eb13d93fbefc4c7285edef537a9fb3e21339f7a3b37a179eeb150db8d726c1b.png)\n\nHence, the set $Z=X\\times Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nZ={(5,r),(5,s),(5,t),(10,r),(10,s),(10,t)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287796 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186287365 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287796 #edb/ref 1069 "q-182022" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287796 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287796 #edb/ref 1071 "For the sets $Z={-3,6,-9}$ and $Y=Z\\times Z,$ determine which of the following statements are true.\n\n- $(-3,6,-3)\\in Y$\n- $(-3,-9)\\in Y$\n- $(-9,6)\\in Y$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287796 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1a71b6cc-f717-587b-ac69-3fbfad95bd60" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287796 #edb/ref 1074 "The Cartesian product $Z\\times Z$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $Z$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $Z.$\n\nIn this case, the schematic for ${Z}^{2}=Z\\times Z$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/0c/0c58bf1f025cc4960ce3b9dc8e1bc3bf474a521473833b27d136fd77fd6b814a.png)\n\nHence, the set $Y=Z\\times Z$ is given by\n\n$$\nY={(-3,-3),(-3,6),(-3,-9),(6,-3),(6,6),(6,-9),(-9,-3)(-9,6),(-9,-9)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348490 #edb/ref 1080 "36" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348490 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348490 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "04e51bd9-4d36-5a76-98d7-1e52bb98ec6a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348672 #edb/ref 1080 "18" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348672 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348672 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1ab8ba58-fe6c-5be4-9d1a-7dfd25e803e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349042 #edb/ref 1080 "9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349042 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349042 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "41c40045-c2bf-5d58-935c-d6eeea1554c1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349814 #edb/ref 1080 "6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349814 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186349814 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "98aeffd4-46bd-567d-ae81-6a8491d47731" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350646 #edb/ref 1080 "11" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350646 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350646 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fa0b481a-52a4-5310-a133-a9ed3e13b778" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350855 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186348490 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350855 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186348672 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350855 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186349042 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350855 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186349814 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350855 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186350646 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350855 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350855 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186350855 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/